 "notes": "Hin Daeng (Red Rock), a boulder pinnacle 70 km offshore whose three tops just break the surface, with the ridge towards Hin Muang; sides and depths from Phuket Dive Guide: sheer soft-coral wall to 60-70 m+ on the south-west, gentler slope on the east, a sand channel on the north separating the coral outcrop used as a manta cleaning station. The site coordinates (an OSM reef node at 7.3676, 98.8758) sit 24 km north-east of the real pinnacle; the origin here is the OSM dive-site node at 7.1490, 98.8236, which agrees with divezone. Positions are approximate.",
